<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 442)</h2>
<p><b>The wave is part of the note.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Voice notes now record your pointer.</b> Wave the cursor at the thing you're talking about — playback retraces it as an orange ring, in time with your voice, on every seat, and it burns into movie exports that hold on voice notes.</li>
<li><b>Paste a session key anywhere.</b> The Shared Review panel takes a review link (or the bare session id and key) — paste and Join.</li>
<li><b>Export All Annotated Frames covers the whole session</b>; "Current clip only" narrows it.</li>
<li>Fixed: live presence (pointers and in-progress strokes from peers) never actually rendered in the native viewport. It does now.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
